WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
KOTORIBAKO

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.090
A kotoribako is a wooden mosaic
that is made of squares

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.010
approximately 8 inches per side.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.470
WOODEN MOSAIC

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.260
It's a box that can't be opened
unless the correct procedure is followed.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.050
It's a magical item
used to curse people to death.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.760
CURSE

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.760
KILL

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.770
Those that are near where the box is placed
have all their internal organs ripped apart,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.520
INTERNAL ORGAN

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.180
and cough up blood as they die.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.520
BLOOD

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.770
Only women and children
are affected by it.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.230
They say it originated around 1860

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.190
and supposedly was created
to curse the village headman to death,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.860
as that village was suffering
from heavy taxes.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.570
As long as it's buried
in the house's yard,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.700
all the women and children
will die one after another,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.120
and all the descendants will perish.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.740
In other words, a kotoribako is defined
as the box that takes children.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.790
To make one,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:43.370
the box must be filled with a female beast's
blood, then left alone for an entire week.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.500
FEMALE BEAST'S BLOOD

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.040
Before the blood all dries up,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.090
a body part from the child that has been
sacrificed must be placed within.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.920
A BODY PART

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.510
The body part to use
depends on the age of the child.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:54.470
For infants, the umbilical cord,
the index finger joint or blood is used.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.510
INDEX FINGER

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.050
For children seven and under,
the index finger joint and lifeblood.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.180
For children ten and under,
only the index finger joint.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.690
The name of the box depends on
the sacrifices in it. One sacrifice is an ippou.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.770
SACRIFICE

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.690
Two makes nihou, three makes sanpou
and four makes shippou.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.070
And if there are eight sacrifices,
it's called a hakkai.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.900
If any more sacrifices are offered,
the box will become dangerously strong.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.700
Depending on the situation, the curse
is said to last over a hundred years.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.240
Nasty... Pretty nasty...

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.450
Gamon, you are the site owner
of an occultic round-up blog, right?

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.210
Don't you have a tolerance
for scary stories?

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.080
I-I'm not scared or anything!

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.670
<i>By the way, this is really something
I shouldn't be telling you.</i>

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.670
TOUKO

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.210
But the information I got from a lead
who has connections to Mumu

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:36.050
points to one of those kotoribakos
somewhere in Kichijoji.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.510
Wha... Kichijoji is way too cursed!

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.800
<i>Look here, you guys.</i>

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.560
<i>A kotoribako is something
that is absolutely no joke.</i>

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.270
<i>Don't think that you can
easily find one. Got that?</i>

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.490
Ryo-tas won't be able to go
to the bathroom tonight!

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.700
More like, Myu-pom,

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.290
why are you so worried
about this kotoribako?

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.170
I... think I want to go look
for it as soon as possible.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.960
It is only folklore.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.710
We can't immediately find out
if it exists or not.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.300
Searching doesn't show
anything, either.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.670
If this really is a book of prediction,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:42.430
A DARK WATER'S BOTTOM

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.840
maybe there is a hint
of some sort drawn in here...

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.470
A hint, huh?

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.220
That's not an ordinary doujinshi.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.560
It does have a lot of information in it.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.100
Something that looks like it...

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.060
A shrine appears in this story.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.940
In other words,
the kotoribako is at a shrine!

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.190
That's too easy.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.190
We should do everything we can.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.190
There are three shrines in Kichijoji.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.110
The Kyokkou Shrine,

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.320
the Musashino Shichimangu

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.070
and Toeda Shrine.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.780
I believe there's one
inside Inokashira Park, as well?

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.030
You're talking about Tenzaisama, right?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.030
INOKASHIRA TENZAITEN

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.830
I've been there before.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.410
I wonder if we can narrow it down?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.620
It's a distinct art style.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.330
It's not like she traced
a photograph, either.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.630
Only if the torii guard frame
was drawn,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.960
we'd have been able
to narrow it down.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.670
Different shrines have different shapes
for the torii guard frames.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.010
There are roughly 60 different variations.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.430
What? Seriously?
I totally didn't know that.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.510
But there are no torii guard frames
drawn within this doujinshi.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.720
The shrine grounds
are drawn pretty spaciously,

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.310
maybe it's the Musashino Shichimangu.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.560
This title... "The Two Gods of Fortune."

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.020
Making a doujinshi out of gods
of fortune... That's beyond imagination!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.650
Perhaps this is alluding
to the Seven Gods of Good Fortune?

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.860
If so, don't you think Tenzaisama
in Inokashira Park is a bit fishy after all?

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:48.120
But these two aren't drawn with any
characteristics of the gods of good fortune.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.490
They're normal handsome guys.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.410
Wait, wasn't Tenzaisama
a temple and not a shrine?

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.830
Oh, was that so?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.880
I do not think there was
a torii guard frame, either.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:00.050
That means... maybe we were mistaken
to think with only shrines in mind.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.010
What is it?

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.550
If we add temples, the number
of possible locations goes up to nine.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.680
Try searching with "Seven Gods
of Good Fortune," "temple" and "Kichijoji."

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.680
Let's see... Oh, looks like
there's one every January.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.680
Kichijoji Seven Gods of Good Fortune rounds

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.180
I didn't know they had something like this.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.350
Let's see... Inokashira Tenzaiten,

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.190
Inokashira Tenzaiten

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.230
Musashino Shichimangu

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.100
Musashino Shichimangu, Taiyouji,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:15.940
Taiyouji

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:16.730
Taihousenji

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.440
Taihousenji, Anmeiji, Hitsugitaisha...

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.310
Anmeiji

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:17.940
Hitsugitaisha

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.190
Six places? Aren't there
Seven Gods of Good Fortune?

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.490
I wonder why they're missing one—

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:22.940
Anmeiji

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.530
It's Anmeiji.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.160
It's the Witch!

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.660
Kurenaino Aria!

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.240
K-Kurenaino Aria?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.830
You really did come to curse me!
It was a mistake after all!

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:37.290
Because I realized the truth hidden
within Ririka Nishizono's doujinshi!

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.630
Kurenaino Aria, her accomplice, has come
to curse me to death with black magic!

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.170
It's too perfect a story!

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.050
Sarai, her job is to curse people to death
as the black magic agent!

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.510
Calm down, Gamon!
There are no such things as curses!

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:48.180
But...

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.890
Ririka Nishizono is someone
I have absolutely no knowledge of.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.480
But what you were talking
about just now

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.020
was something I was listening to
with much interest.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.860
Even though you just got here?

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.820
The one who was listening
was my partner...

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:02.860
the Devil...

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.240
How ridiculous! Black magic and devils?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.290
You've brought fantasy into this world,
and furthermore, you use it as your trade.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.580
At that point, it goes
from shocked to disdain!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.710
And on top of that,
you say your partner is the devil?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.420
Looking at you... You are still young.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.540
Limit your jokes to your sense of fashion
which seems to be cosplay.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:25.170
If you can converse with the devil,
can you summon him right here and now?

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.630
I'd love to meet one for once

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.470
and hear memories of Greek myths
for future reference.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.020
It's rather well done for a magic trick!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.100
I've seen the likes of this on TV, as well,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.230
but how did you do this
without taking time to prepare—

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.410
This is your penalty
for trying to test black magic.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.700
No... for trying to test me.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.370
Tried to test you? Penalty?

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.830
Like how we requested a black magic
agent by lying that I was two-timing?

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.250
I knew it! I'm going to be murdered!

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.800
Like that light bulb just now,
my head will burst!

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.380
Anyway, isn't it better for you
to hurry on your way?

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.800
Normally, there is one god
for each shrine or temple.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:16.560
However, in Anmeiji, there are two gods
of fortune. Bishamanten and Jurouzen.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.440
Two gods of fortune...
So kotoribako is in Anmeiji?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.900
This world is full of ill will.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.860
And all those wills
are connected to one will.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.740
It looks like it was merely
our misunderstanding.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.070
Who are you speaking to?

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:32.030
It was more unmerciful and cruel
than the will of the devil.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.410
An existence of pure white
that knows no pain.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.450
The one that embraces the large box...

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.330
The one that embraces
the box at Anmeiji...

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.080
is a boy.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.800
A boy whose hair,
and everything else, is pure white.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.670
Myu-pom!

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.770
So, what will happen now?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.570
That guy...

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.650
Is something wrong?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.740
I've seen him before... To think
he'd be at a place like this...

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:16.450
My friend who's gone missing sent me
one last text with a photo attachment.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:21.160
The picture was of the road painted by
the sunset, her shadow and a trading card.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.420
It had unnatural white lines of light.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:26.420
That alone makes it sound pretty bad.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:29.420
And one word, kotoriba,
was written with it.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.420
KOTORIBA

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.630
Kotoriba...

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.680
Kotoribako?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.140
If the boy Aria spoke of
is at Anmeiji...

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.640
He may know something!

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.150
What's that sound?

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.900
I hear it from over there.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.200
Who are you?

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.790
A white human... really was here!

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.370
Wait! That guy is trouble!

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:04.580
Hey, hey, Miss.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.550
It looks like I made a mistake
making the box.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.840
There was something
like an instruction manual online,

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.050
but I didn't read it well,
so I couldn't help it.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.760
But you don't normally
read stuff like that, right?

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.470
Does anyone seriously read them?

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.640
About 80% of Japanese people build stuff

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.930
without reading
the instruction manuals, right?

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:22.640
Chi...

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.060
I smell blood.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.570
Hey, do you know my friend?
She goes by "Chi."

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:31.990
Her name is Chizu Kawabata.
She's a first year at Seimei High School—

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:31.990
I need a sacrifice.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.990
I need a sacrifice inside the kotoribako.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:42.160
It was written online that the sacrifice
had to be someone that everyone loves.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:45.370
Oh, but I'm still a minor so this won't
be a crime. After all, I'm a minor.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.790
I was taught that there was
someone suited to being the sacrifice.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.130
Something about a high school girl
who was attracting lots of attention.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.920
I thought that someone like that
would be perfect for my sacrifice.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.420
Hey!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.380
But I think I made a mistake.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.140
The sacrifice...

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.260
Even if I make a mistake,
I'm a minor so it won't be a crime.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.600
Hey, what exactly is inside that box—

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:03.600
What's wrong?

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.390
After all, I'm a minor so they're not
going to prosecute any crimes.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.060
I-I'll call the cops!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.730
The police? Why?

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:13.110
I've been telling you that I'm a minor
so it won't be a crime.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.690
Answer my question!

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:17.410
If you want to know that much,
I'll give you this box.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.530
I'm partially done making it.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.040
Myu...

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.370
So, it was you.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.250
Oh, hold it, wait!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.250
Why did he know your name?

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:32.590
I don't know.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.630
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.260
<i>I'm sure to regret this if I look.</i>

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.260
<i>I know that, but...</i>

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.700
Dammit, no good!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.160
We lost sight of him.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.530
Myu-pom! What are you doing?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.200
Nooo!

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.210
Those with life will always die someday.
As seen in zen dialogues.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.460
Until now, human life was finite.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.590
With the development
of medical technology,

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.840
that span has drastically
increased compared to before.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.350
Yet, it's still at levels which are
a far cry from everlasting life.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:27.350
However, this theory we've discovered
from years of research and investigation,

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:32.150
named "New World System,"
makes that infinite life a reality!

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.810
NEW WORLD SYSTEM

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.570
Life is memories and consciousness...

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:38.990
It's constructed by electrical energy
that has information about each person.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.280
And those who've left their physical bodies
after being affected by something

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.580
are called spiritual or astral bodies,

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.120
and have been treated
as mysterious phenomena.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:51.000
Their preservation and retention
was the only largest problem until now.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.790
But we've finally found the way!

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.880
What you'd call
"advancing into the spirit realm"

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.260
that was unearthed
from the legacy of Nikola Tesla...

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:01.300
However, unless we solve
the problem of the "prison of time,"

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.390
it's nothing more
than a castle in the air.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.760
Exactly.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.180
Even if we were to eternally preserve
a soul, it's useless if it merely exists.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:11.100
Synchronization between
absolute time and relative time...

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.690
Because of that,
you can say a person is alive.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.490
Please rest assured. You can say
that it's already been resolved.

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:22.860
An important hint was hidden in this
unpublished paper from Professor Hashigami.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:26.240
"A World and Time
Which Turn into the Spirit Realm."

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:30.210
That's right. With these marvelous
research results left behind by the dead,

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:33.790
it's finally possible for us to escape
from the "prison of time."

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.750
If this had been shared with the public,

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.880
it would've overturned
common sense of mankind.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.760
Of course, not every answer
was written within it.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.890
If we can adjust our research
trajectory based on this,

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:49.270
we may be able to synchronize
the time of the spirit world to our world.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:52.940
What we'll see beyond that...
In other words, we obtain the spirit realm.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.440
March 6th (Sunday)

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.190
So you don't enter your
big brother's room all that often.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.440
Right.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.490
Then what about cleaning?

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.530
You can't possibly leave it alone
with all the dust piling up...

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:07.280
Well, I'm thinking that isn't the case.
This shop looks all nice and tidy, too.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.290
It's a shop with a good atmosphere!

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.750
Do you need something from me?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.080
Oh, well...

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.210
Actually, there was a corpse that
came out from the box found at Anmeiji

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:19.210
that was all messed up,
like mincemeat.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:21.260
We've identified one person
from the items left behind.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:24.340
It was Chizu Kawabata,
one of the local high school girls.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:28.720
Actually, there also were blood
and muscle fragments from other people.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.180
But we're waiting for identification
for those. Do you have any questions?

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.390
I do.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.650
Why are you taking the time
to tell me such a story?

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:38.650
Well, since you know a lot
about black magic and curses,

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.820
I thought you might know something.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:44.490
Black magic is my specialty,
but why me?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.360
Aren't there other people
who are just as famous?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:50.740
Oh, well... When I looked up
the Kichijoji phone book for black magic,

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.370
I saw the phone number for here.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.670
We don't list our number
in the phone book.

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:57.290
Oh, you caught me out?

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:00.340
By the way, didn't you curse
someone recently, as well?

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.960
And by "someone," you mean...

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.300
I wasn't pointing
at a particular someone.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:06.800
It's like... Did you have a request
with tons of tenacity and grudges

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.850
rolled up into a giant heap?

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.470
For instance, a large lump sum
paid out in cash...

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:15.100
Or some hair was delivered to you
with a death wish of the owner of the hair.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.980
I spoke with you the other day
regarding Professor Hashigami.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.480
You should be done with me already.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.400
Oh, you're so indifferent.
And while I'm at it, one more thing...

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:23.490
Minase...

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:24.990
Yes?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.110
- Do you know of kodoku?
- No.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.990
A simple explanation would be...

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.830
that it's a spell where you pack various
types of insects into a sealable urn,

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:36.620
and have them kill and eat each other,
and create the one strongest insect.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.920
I know not of it. This is a shop
that deals with Western magic.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.750
Oh, that means you know
that kodoku is magic from the East.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.420
Gimme a break, you said earlier
that you didn't know about it.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:48.890
So, what's the link between the box
you found at the temple and this kodoku?

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:52.100
Do you mean that those found
within the box were victims of kodoku?

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:56.430
Oh no, it didn't seem like kodoku was
created by making humans kill each other.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.060
The corpses showed no vital reaction,

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.020
so it seemed like they were
chopped up after they were dead.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.610
But there was something
that stuck to my mind.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.190
If you use the insect that survived
the kodoku method as the divine objective,

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.280
the effects of the spell
supposedly becomes immense.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.950
Fighting deathmatches
with the other insects, eating their corpses,

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.580
slurping their excrements, the filthy one
that persistently lingered to life...

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:14.790
The effects of the curse
will double or more!

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.370
That is quite interesting.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.710
Boy, you make it sound
like you have no interest.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:19.920
Please leave.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:22.250
Then one last thing, if I may?

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:23.750
What is it?

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.630
How did you know
that Chizu Kawabata was at Anmeiji?

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:30.550
The devil had told me
that strong karma was gathering there.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:33.560
So your spells use devils as the medium.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:36.560
Where did you meet this devil?
Is it trustworthy?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.230
Weren't you done
with your questions?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:41.020
Well now, this will really be the last one.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:42.020
In reality...

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.400
You don't believe in devils, do you?

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:47.860
Ria Minase, you were in love
with your big brother, right?

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.530
Big brother and little sister...

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.280
That's a good thing. I wish I had
a cute little sister who loved me, as well!

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.910
What do you want to say?

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.330
The relationship between you,
Minase, and the devil

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.040
seems to be the reverse
compared to black magic I know.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.630
For example, Minase, you're the servant
and the devil is the master?

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:05.340
So maybe you sought a new master
who'd take your brother's place

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.300
and settled into what you have now...

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.590
No, I think you've resigned
yourself to do so.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:14.350
You didn't want knowledge in black magic
nor a minion that faithfully executes it.

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:18.220
You wanted something that accepts you
being there as an uncertain, vague self.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:21.640
It's the same as the depressed people
repeating acts of self-harm.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:22.350
Get out...

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:25.270
You want a being that unconditionally
affirms your existence.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.900
If that condition is met, you don't care
what it is... Even if it was the devil—

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:30.400
That surprised me!

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.450
That just now was obstruction
of justice, you know?

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.830
Leave now... Leave!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.170
Excuse me. I stepped in a bit too far.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:46.960
Please forget that act of disrespect as
an exchange with that obstruction of justice.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:47.670
See you.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.680
Don't get too absorbed in this...

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.060
Grim Reaper.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:09.030
And that's why you got rid of the 256
from the first generation,

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.820
now that they're no longer needed?

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:13.990
Development of any wonder drug
needs clinical trials.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:16.990
Even if effects of healing difficult
illnesses are solidified in theory,

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:21.040
if you don't test it, neither the problems
nor how to deal with them can be found.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.790
They are what you can
call valuable sacrifices

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.210
in order to welcome
the new world and era.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:29.250
I did say that it was no good
to be jealous while doing nothing.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.840
I also told you to take
countermeasures

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.380
concerning the bugs
in the 256 of the first generation.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:37.300
We'd thought it wouldn't be too big
an issue if we used a bit of brute force.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:40.430
That's why we prepared
all this flourishing of the occult.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:44.100
Nowadays, when you turn the TV on,
it's always occult, occult and more occult.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.560
But still, it was a bit too much
to kill them all at once!

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.650
And in such a way that's so noticeable!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:52.990
The countermeasures were the result
of putting highest priority to the objective.

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.910
<i>You know, how long
are you going to be doing that?</i>

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.240
Shut up.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.910
<i>Don't you have something else
to do right now?</i>

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.660
<i>Can you leave her alone like this?</i>

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.420
<i>She just collapsed
right afterwards, right?</i>

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:12.010
There's nothing I can do for Myu-pom
right now... or rather, this is the only thing.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.670
<i>Isn't it better to leave
something like that with someone else?</i>

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:19.760
For now, the names of 43 people match.
In the end, all of them should match.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.430
<i>More than a list like that is the key...
the key! Isn't that more important?</i>

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:25.350
Of course the key is important, too.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:29.810
I walked all over and looked,
but I couldn't find a keyhole at all.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.190
So, this is
what I should be doing now.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.280
This is the only thing for me.

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.070
Man, I'm tired!

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:42.740
How is it? Is there any progress
in that case at Ino Park?

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:46.000
Hello? Can you hear me?

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.210
Um, excuse me, did something happen?

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:53.380
Or is everyone pulling a prank on me?
That's pretty outdated.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:57.840
Bullying like this as an adult isn't
a joke anymore. Bullying is unfashionable!

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.930
That's a bit old, too.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.270
We're back.

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.480
Hey, can you listen
for a bit, Shinoyama?

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.560
Everyone is bullying me.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:10.860
Hey now, are you serious?

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.230
More like, why are both of you
wearing mourning suits?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.280
Are you coming
from a funeral or something?

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.860
At least listen to what I have to say!

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:19.070
You know...

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.830
I don't know what you're so irritated
about, but at least hear—

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:36.460
Editor-in-chief,

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:39.590
the corpse that was cut into pieces,
boxed up and found at Anmeiji...

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:41.890
It apparently was Miyuu Aikawa's friend.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.060
Editor-in-chief?

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:48.810
HASHIGAMI

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:49.890
I'm home.

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:53.570
Mom?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:55.900
Mom!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:06.410
MITAKA CITY MASS SUICIDE
200 VICTIMS FOUND IN INOKASHIRA PARK

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:02.700
<i>The police have announced more victims
that have been identified.</i>

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:06.120
<i>Now, we have 200 victims
who have been identified,</i>

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:10.210
<i>but the remaining 56
still remain unidentified.</i>

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.750
<i>The latest victims to be identified
are the following.</i>

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.880
<i>Tadashi Iguchi. Yoko Ishizuka.</i>

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:21.010
There we go, that completes
70 people's worth. Let's see...

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:21.010
<i>Mitsuko Edo. Toyohiko Ohba.
Yasumi Okada.</i>

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.010
<i>Yuta Gamon.</i>

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.760
<i>Souka Kukimoto. Kotone Kuzuhara.</i>

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:26.390
Hey, Zonko!

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:28.480
<i>Masumi Koba. Rie Sagae.</i>

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:27.310
Did you hear that just now?

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:30.020
I-I'm a victim!

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:32.770
<i>Seiji Sasaki. Nozomi Tsujimoto.</i>

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.770
This is rather funny!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.070
From the code words in the ceiling
and from the news on TV,

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.610
my name was called out
at the exact same time!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.900
What in the world is this?

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:40.700
<i>Jeez.</i>

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.200
<i>You found it, huh?</i>

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:48.160
You're kidding, right?

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:33.480
The transition into the second phase
was supposed to be done incrementally!

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:36.940
You ignored that and killed off
all of the first generation! That's reckless!

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:39.190
In the first place,
the Scandium Project—

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:42.440
Experimental guinea pigs
sometimes bite humans if let loose.

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:46.570
One is free to say their specs were high,
but I don't think that way.

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:50.330
Guinea pigs that have gone wild
can cause the entire project to collapse.

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:53.660
We were able to confirm the bugs
in only a few of the first generation,

00:22:53.660 --> 00:22:55.410
but that was indeed a premonition.

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:57.580
With the passing of time,
those numbers had the possibility

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:59.420
to jump up into double and triple digits.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:03.760
Think of it as a few guinea pigs
getting sick within the same cage.

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:07.630
If you let it be, all the guinea pigs
in the cage would've gotten infected.

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:09.260
Your reasoning makes sense, but—

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:10.930
That number all at once is impossible!

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:14.390
If you randomly chose patients
as experiment subjects, that much risk is—

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:15.770
That is way too arbitrary
of a decision and execution!

00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:18.020
How many people did it take
to deal with it after the fact?

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.600
You possibly can't be oblivious!

00:23:19.600 --> 00:23:22.070
We won't trouble you, Mr. Hatoyama.

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:25.530
Mind control based on the occult
is working well enough.

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:28.200
The atmosphere
of the situation is a factor

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.990
that takes priority over all else
for the citizens of this country.

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:34.490
No matter how abnormal
the situation becomes. Correct?

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:38.920
With the annulment of the first generation
whose purpose has ended,

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.840
we'll move the plan onto Phase 2.

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:53.390
Hello?
